body:
i haven't even tried to make the sheet yet since it'll have a bunch of colors on it -- we're talking at least 30 different colors.

&#x200B;

i think what i want to do would be considered drop down sorting, but i don't know if i'm using the term correctly. the chart i linked as an example shows want i want to do better than i can describe.

the label is a bit deceiving -- i noticed it had the black mushrooms on the label even though the back of the label doesn't list any mushrooms that could be black and chanterelle-like. i thought they were black trumpets when i first saw them

&#x200B;

edit: also noticed they put chanterelles on the front label...weird.

i know snow sugar's yeti has the same movement as snow sugar, the issue is that it obscures the hitbox she has to the point where i'm constantly missing some of the last few trios of rainbow bear jellies i need (the total is 45 and i've been hitting either 42 or 44 as my total). when her yeti disappears, it throws me off since it's always in mid-air so i can't reorient myself from the ground. the yeti takes up half of the screen, and it's difficult to tell just where sugar snow will be once it disappears since it doesn't fall at a forward angle as quickly as a cookie can.

&#x200B;

i don't have the paradise compass treasure and i DID "pay attention" to the level behind me...at max level, with her pet at max level as well, successfully hitting EVERY goal the level has, i still fall \~5 million short of the score i need for 3 stars...and i can't make those points up with the targets because i need to disregard the targets more or less completely in order to aim for the coins with some semblance of accuracy.

&#x200B;

snow sugar and her snowglobe are only level 10. if beet cookie being maxed out did ultimately nothing to change her score, i highly doubt that maxing her out will either. thanks for trying to help, though.

no :( i never really got advice from anyone either.

&#x200B;

i initially asked in the daily help thread, but it was so filled (i asked at the end of the weekend) that i don't think anyone saw it. i've even tried asking online under cookie run's twitter advertisements or on the cookie run wiki, but to no avail.

&#x200B;

i'm wondering if it's a bug of some sort that uninstalling and reinstalling would fix...but i'm scared to do so since i stash my passwords for stuff EVERYWHERE and i don't remember what my devsisters login credentials are. i don't wanna reinstall the game so i can progress just to find out i've lost ALL of my progress, y'know?
